  set:  # 656c
    title: "stable_id is None on every function of whole languages (clojure/elixir/erlang/haskell/ocaml/zig): the by-kind backstop has no default arm and those producers never compute one"  # 656c
    description: "Found by the 2026-08-01 self-analysis run that closed META-niguz (dev fa7ae4e388). META-niguz's criterion was 0 SYNTHESIZED-node identity gaps and that is met; these are ordinary analyzer-emitted nodes (real origin, real hgfp2 fingerprint, no protocol_origin, real path and language), so the Class-B / synthetic backstops are not the responsible path.\n\nORIGINAL SYMPTOM (self-map): stable_id None on 8 nodes at filing, 11 at dev 134a06d505 (55,141 nodes): json/package 3 (incl. the PRODUCTION path packages/htrac-frontend/package.json), proto/message 2, toml/package 2, proto/method 1, csharp/property 1, erlang/function 1, bash/alias 1. All but the htrac one are under fixture paths.\n\nWHOLE-LANGUAGE SCOPE: the erlang/function node is not a one-off. A tiny fixture survey (2-3 functions per file, dev 134a06d505) gives stable_id None on EVERY function in clojure 2/2, elixir 2/2, erlang 3/3, haskell 2/2, ocaml 2/2, zig 2/2 (none_cohort_pct 56.52); their module/file nodes are stamped. The self map understates this because those languages appear there only as one-file fixtures. erlang.py never sets stable_id; by grep (heuristic, not verified module by module) 27 analyzer modules that emit function kinds never mention stable_id, incl. commonlisp, fsharp, elm, qml, thrift, gdscript, lean, agda, circom, wolfram, llvm_ir.\n\nMECHANISM (confirmed): the backstop populate_kind_stable_ids (analyze/base.py:1724) dispatches on kind through _KIND_STABLE_ID_FACTORIES (base.py:1701: file/module/dependency/variable/export/project/interface/type, class/struct/enum/trait/protocol/contract, template) and `continue`s on a miss (:1749-1751) — no default arm; its docstring states that as policy. function/method/property/package/message/alias are not in the map, and the producers above never call compute_stable_id. This is the same shape as META-nomiz's kind='template' residual, fixed as a site rather than a class in PR #15.\n\nA default arm would remove the None values but would NOT give those languages the typed ADR-0035 formula (compute_stable_id / make_typed_stable_id) their sibling analyzers use; the producers need it too.\n\nWHY NO GATE CAUGHT IT: validation_report.stable_id_stats reports collision_rate_pct 0.0 with none_cohort disclosed (ADR-0035 / WI-niluv) but not RATCHETED, so the nulls sit under a report that otherwise reads all-clear. Recurrence test: a property test that every emitted Symbol kind, in every analyzer, resolves to a non-null stable_id. Do NOT close on the self-map none_cohort number alone; registering only the observed kinds reproduces the per-site pattern this item exists to break.\n\nRelated: WI-banod (config-family analyzers stamp a composite id), INV-dulah.\nRevised 2026-09-30 from the premise check (see discussion)."  # 656c
- op: discuss  # c1af
  at: '2026-10-01T14:08:20Z'  # c1af
  by: agent  # c1af
  actor: jgstern_agent  # c1af
  clock: 5  # c1af
  nonce: c1af  # c1af
  message: "WORK DONE 2026-10-01 (concurrent run, local branch jgstern-agent/fix/motiz, commit 41eb17ca29, NOT pushed or merged).\nFIX: populate_kind_stable_ids (analyze/base.py) now has a DEFAULT arm. A kind outside _KIND_STABLE_ID_FACTORIES on a Symbol WITH a language gets make_declaration_stable_id(kind, language, path, name), the existing backstop shape. language=None stand-ins are still skipped (their identity belongs to make_synthetic_symbol_identity). Producer values are never overridden. Same-file same-name siblings share the key and are split by the existing split_within_file_stable_id_collisions (ADR-0035 §1 occurrence index). Before the fix, 139 of the 154 registered kinds were outside the map. ADR-0014 §5b amended in place: its \"kinds not in the factory table are left untouched\" clause is the policy this changes. OWNER DECISION POINT at integration.\nTESTS: core property test over every kind in the symbol-kind registry plus an unregistered kind (5 of 7 new unit tests red on dev, green on the branch; the language=None guard test was mutation-checked red). End-to-end survey tests: lang-common (clojure/elixir/erlang/haskell/ocaml, incl. the Elixir Demo.main/0 and /1 split) and lang-extended1 (zig), red on a dev snapshot and green on the branch. Targeted smart-test: 15079 passed, 4 xfailed, 0 failed; changed source files at 100% coverage.\nMEASURED (sampled corpus fixture: up to 4 small files per language from ~/whole_bunch_of_repos plus hand snippets, 3,176 symbols, dev 4376f204f1 vs branch): stable_id_stats none_cohort 525 (16.53%) -> 0; 0 existing non-null values changed; same node-id set; 0 collision groups and 0 per-file collision groups after. 69 (language, kind) pairs filled. NOT measured: the self-map and any full corpus repo.\nNOT DONE: the producers still do not compute the ADR-0035 formula. For clojure/elixir/erlang/haskell/ocaml that is information-neutral: compute_stable_id finds no params node and no decorator node on their functions. Zig: 1 of 2 functions had a params node, and zig has no overloading. The residual is filed as WI-tusad-rilub-jipuv-tibum-rijab-tahut-kijov-toral (P3), with the measured list and the C-family declarator caveat."  # c1af
